---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import JournalPromptGenerator from "../components/JournalPromptGenerator.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import storyHero from "../assets/your-story-write-hero-quill-v2.jpg";
import journalSetting from "../assets/your-story-journaling.jpg";
import "../styles/stories-page.css";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Free Writing Prompts for Self-Discovery | Dare to Break Free"
  description="Explore writing for self-discovery with Kali Harmen. Try free writing prompts designed to spark curiosity and see where your thoughts take you."
>
  <header class="stories-hero">
    <Image
      class="stories-hero__image"
      src={storyHero}
      alt="A teal and black quill over a pale lavender watercolor background"
      widths={[640, 960, 1280, 1600, 2000, 2400]}
      sizes="100vw"
      format="webp"
      quality={82}
      loading="eager"
      fetchpriority="high"
      decoding="async"
    />
    <div class="stories-container">
      <h1>Writing for Self-Discovery</h1>
      <p class="stories-lede">See where a question takes you.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="stories-section stories-section--explore" aria-labelledby="stories-know-heading">
    <div class="stories-container stories-split stories-knowing">
      <figure class="stories-reading-image">
        <Image
          src={journalSetting}
          alt="Kali writing in a notebook at home"
          widths={[480, 720, 960, 1200, 1600]}
          sizes="(max-width: 600px) calc(100vw - 2 * var(--page-gutter)), (max-width: 900px) min(70vw, 30rem), 45vw"
          format="webp"
          quality={82}
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        />
      </figure>
      <div class="stories-prose">
        <h2 id="stories-know-heading">Getting to know ourselves</h2>
        <p>I've often wondered how much of our struggles come from being disconnected from ourselves. We're so busy getting on with life, responding to what's happening around us and doing what needs to be done that it's surprisingly easy to lose touch with what we actually feel or want.</p>
        <p>And even when we do have a bit of time to ourselves, how often do we spend it without some sort of distraction?</p>
        <p>I think we can become quite good at avoiding ourselves without even realising we're doing it.</p>
        <p>Which brings me to writing as a way in.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="stories-section stories-section--writing" aria-labelledby="stories-invitation-heading">
    <div class="stories-container stories-split stories-invitation">
      <div class="stories-prose">
        <h2 id="stories-invitation-heading">A little time with yourself</h2>
        <p>So, how about giving it a go? You don’t need to be a writer. Just give yourself a few minutes, grab something to write with and see what comes out.</p>
        <p>I’ve put together a collection of questions to get you started. Some are playful, others a little more thought-provoking, and some might take you into uncomfortable territory.</p>
        <p>Starting with a question can take you somewhere you wouldn’t necessarily have gone on your own. You might end up writing a load of waffle (it was in your head anyway!), or stumble across something that makes you think, ‘Hang on, where did that come from?’</p>
        <p>Spend five minutes with one or get completely carried away. If a question doesn’t interest you, pick another. And if something feels too much, leave it. It’s up to you what you choose to explore.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="stories-writing__prompt">
        <JournalPromptGenerator compact={true} />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</BaseLayout>
